<title>SINGAPORE: India awards Vizag naphtha to Yukong.</title>
<headline>India awards Vizag naphtha to Yukong.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has awarded its tender to sell 27,000 tonnes of low aromatic naphtha (LAN) from Vizag to South Korean refiner Yukong Ltd at around $30.00 per tonne below Japanese spot quotes, industry sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The tender which closed January 30 and was valid until January 31, offered the cargo off the east coast on a free-on-board basis February 9-11.</p>
<p>IOC's last tender from Visag, for a cargo lifting Janaury 5-7 was cancelled due to higher domestic demand.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-8703086)</p>
